!! [[0.12.0|https://crosseye.github.io/TW5-JSON_Convert/0.12.0/]]
//Released 2026-09-28//

Bindings could see one field of the current record, and a transform could see one value.  Everything asked for after 0.11 — the import time, a padding width, the other fields of the record, a lookup in the wiki — was a request for something else.  This release closes that gap without adding a second binding language: context paths and transform parameters.

* ''Imported tiddlers now have dates.''  ''Apply'' stamps `created` and `modified` at the moment of import, unless the profile binds them, so imports appear under Recent.  A new profile key, `stamp`, lists what to fill: `[]` opts out, `creator` and `modifier` opt in.  Overwriting an existing tiddler never changes its `created` or `creator` by stamping.  This changes what every import has produced so far, which is why it leads.
* ''Context paths.''  `{{@now}}` is the import time in TiddlyWiki's date format, `{{@counter}}` the record's position counting from 1, `{{@record}}` the whole record as JSON text (or `{{@record.field}}` to reach into it).  The Browse modal lists them above the record tree.
* ''Transform parameters,'' in the operand syntax you know from filters: `{{id|zero-pad[3]}}`, `{{s|replace[from],[to]}}`.  Six new built-ins take them: `zero-pad`, `default`, `prefix`, `suffix`, `replace`, and `pluck[key]`, which turns an array of objects into a title list of one property — Discourse tags, CSL authors.  A malformed parameter is a validation error that spells out the syntax.
* ''Custom transforms see the record.''  JavaScript bodies get `params`, `record` and `counter` beside `value`; wikitext bodies get `param`, `params`, `record` (as JSON text) and `counter`.  A lookup can now key on two fields.  Existing transforms are unaffected: `value` is still first and alone.
* ''`default` works on missing paths.''  A token whose path is absent used to skip its transforms and yield ''; transforms now run with an undefined value (the warning stays), so `{{x|default[none]}}` does what it says.
* ''Quoted path segments.''  A key containing `.`, `[`, `]` or `/`, or starting with `@`, is written `["like.this"]`.  Such keys were unreachable before; the pickers now emit the quoted form, and the tree's "(unsupported key)" note is gone.
* ''Messages count from 1.''  "record 3 produced an empty title" now means the third record.  The `recordIndex` field on error objects stays 0-based for code.
* ''Also fixed.''  Rendering a path after a `..` segment omitted the separator (`...foo`); nothing had rendered one before.  The Console's ''Edit'' and ''Generate importer…'' buttons and the editor now work on a profile that ships inside a pack, which they refused as "not a tiddler".
* ''Documentation.''  Token and path grammar references; the built-ins table; the custom-transform pages; recipes for stamping the import time, numbering records, and looking up a related tiddler at import; a `stamp` section under Profiles.

Importers generated by 0.11 keep working.  A 0.11 runtime given a 0.12 profile that uses `@` paths or parameters reports `binding-bad-token` or `unknown-transform` rather than misbehaving.
